ompensation.","ROE of 6% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (4.1x equity multiplier).","It spends 5.7% of revenue on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.8x net debt to EBITDA ($1.0B of cash against $1.2B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 1.3x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.39 in the distress zone.","The value-trap profile is elevated (63/100); see the breakdown below."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 8.2% over 3 years, 25.6% over 5 years and 2.4% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 28%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Margins are contracting (-2.8% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 13%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 4.3% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 29, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.4%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 10.4% a year to shareholders (10.4% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.3% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 34.7% of the float, 6.2 days to cover."],"people":["With about 2,455 employees, each generates about $770K of revenue, 2.0x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 8.1% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $66K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.9M (2x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $44K per employee."]},"profile":{"score":31.0,"head":"Red flag: Altman Z in the distress zone (1.39).","pros":["Trades 57% below fair value of $17.15","Revenue grew 25.6%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.8x","P/E 9.4x vs sector 18.7x","P/FCF 5.3x vs sector 16.5x"],"cons":["ROIC 6.8% vs WACC 7.0%","Interest coverage only 1.3x